// Motorcycle weighting — the deltas on top of car.json, not a whole model.
//
// GraphHopper has no motorcycle encoder, so `moto` rides on the car model and
// adjusts priority: motorways are dull on a bike and this app exists to avoid
// them, tracks and poor surfaces are unpleasant on two wheels, and the app's
// own round-trip planner biases toward curvature on top of whatever comes back
// here.
//
// This is a plausible motorcycle route, not a tuned motorcycle profile — same
// caveat the docker/dev config has carried since it was written.
//
// Layering: config.yml lists `custom_model_files: [car.json, moto.json]` and
// GraphHopper merges them in order. There is NO `"base"` key in a custom model
// — CustomModel's only fields are speed, priority, areas, distance_influence,
// heading_penalty and turn_penalty — so the file list is how a model inherits.
//
// That car.json is GraphHopper's built-in one, out of the jar, not a file in
// this directory. Checking a copy in here is not an option: GraphHopper refuses
// to start with "Custom model file name 'car.json' is already used for built-in
// profiles" if custom_models.directory holds a file named after a built-in. So
// `car` tracks whatever upstream ships, and only these deltas are ours. For
// reference, the 11.0 built-in is distance_influence 90, priority
// `!car_access -> 0`, speed `limit_to car_average_speed`.
//
// Every encoded value below (road_class, track_type, surface) must be in
// config.yml's graph.encoded_values or the build fails.
//
// GraphHopper 11 also ships its own motorcycle.json + curvature.json, which are
// better tuned than this but need the `curvature` encoded value and ideally
// graph.urban_density. Worth evaluating; deliberately not adopted here, so this
// upgrade changes the GraphHopper version and nothing about the routes.

{
  "priority": [
    { "if": "road_class == MOTORWAY",    "multiply_by": "0.3" },
    { "if": "road_class == TRUNK",       "multiply_by": "0.7" },
    { "if": "road_class == RESIDENTIAL", "multiply_by": "0.8" },
    { "if": "track_type != MISSING",     "multiply_by": "0.2" },
    { "if": "surface == GRAVEL || surface == DIRT || surface == SAND",
      "multiply_by": "0.2" }
  ]
}
